# Atomic Components & shadcn/ui

## Directory structure

Organize `src/components/` by atomic design layer:

```
src/components/
├── ui/          # shadcn primitives (Button, Input, Card, etc.)
├── atoms/       # project-specific single elements
├── molecules/   # small compositions with one responsibility
├── organisms/   # larger self-contained sections
└── templates/   # page layouts that arrange organisms (optional)
```

## Layer responsibilities

| Layer | Purpose | Examples |
|-------|---------|----------|
| `ui/` | shadcn-installed primitives — treat as atoms | `Button`, `Input`, `Card` |
| `atoms/` | custom single-purpose elements not covered by shadcn | `Logo`, `PriceTag` |
| `molecules/` | groups of atoms/ui | `SearchField`, `NavLink` |
| `organisms/` | distinct page sections | `SiteHeader`, `Hero`, `ContactForm` |
| `templates/` | layout shells shared across pages | `MarketingLayout` |

Pages in `src/app/` compose templates or organisms — not raw atoms.

## Import direction

Only import **downward** in the hierarchy:

`templates` → `organisms` → `molecules` → `atoms` → `ui`

Never import an organism from a molecule or atom.

## Prefer shadcn

Before building custom UI from scratch:

1. Check the [shadcn/ui docs](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components) for an existing component.
2. Install it: `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>`
3. Import from `@/components/ui/<component>`.
4. Customize with Tailwind classes and `cn()` — compose in `atoms/` or `molecules/`, don't fork `ui/` files unless the primitive itself must change.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — compose shadcn primitives in a molecule
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input";

export function SearchField() {
  return (
    <div className="flex gap-2">
      <Input placeholder="Search…" />
      <Button type="submit">Search</Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — reinventing a shadcn primitive
export function CustomButton({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return <button className="rounded-md bg-primary px-4 py-2">{children}</button>;
}
```

## When custom components are appropriate

- No shadcn equivalent exists for the primitive.
- The component is business-specific (brand logo, pricing display).
- You are composing existing `ui/` primitives into higher-level pieces.

## File conventions

- PascalCase component names with named exports.
- Colocate stories (`*.stories.tsx`) and tests next to the component.
- Use `@/` path aliases for all imports.
